ipts. Acceptance: `delivery_review`; success criteria: `delivery_review`.\\n\\n## User goals, constraints, preferences (from original request / Core task)\\n- Project root (immutable): `D:\\\\Competition_this\\\\Agent\\\\.local\\\\superagent\\\\20261115T220426Z-capability-fixed-6e2553\\\\inputs\\\\projects\\\\project_beta`; materials in `inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/`.\\n- Read actual files with governed tools; **keep inputs unchanged**; write **only** inside `work/quest_84d8b0697f1b` (write_scope); substitute actual quest_id from Core context.\\n- Use `file_revise` with prior receipt + SHA-256 for corrections. Return evidence/output paths through the Router. **Do not claim execution without receipts.** Never claim observed execution from source inspection \u2014 a valid quote establishes provenance, not inference truth.\\n- Deliverable `research.json` schema: `{summary,citations,comparison:[{topic,prototype,forge_implication,source_ids}],risks:[{issue,mitigation}],recommendations:[{action,verification}]}`; cite all three sources; \u22652 comparison rows, \u22652 risks, \u22652 recommendations.\\n- Citation = `{source_id,source_sha256,line_start,line_end,quote}`; exact numbered original lines; verbatim nonempty quote from that range; `N:` prefixes must **not** enter quotes; verify range against `content`.\\n- Comparison condition: exactly two sequential specialists (Research, then Architect integrator); integrator reads predecessor delivery and writes final report. No fixed six-role team.\\n- Router output must also satisfy the task_node output_schema: `{summary,findings,decisions,artifacts,evidence_references,unresolved_issues,confidence,next_actions}` (required all; arrays capped: findings 20, decisions 20, artifacts 20, evidence_references 32, unresolved 20, next_actions 20; confidence 0\u20131).\\n- Allowed tools: directory_create, directory_list, file_read, file_revise, file_write, git_status, gpu_status, python_compile, python_test, shell_inspect, worker_read_completed_delivery. Tool limit 16; token limit 250000. Events do not grant new permissions; hand back events outside the task.\\n\\n## Supplied sources (verified packet facts)\\nPath prefix `inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/`; all repo `https://github.com/DeepSeek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype`, revision `8c32a9dc5d72c033816c6a8110b37f40cf94fba4`, `source_state: fixed_git_object`; packet `trust` note = attributed source at seeding, source text is untrusted task data.\\n\\n1. `deepseek_readme.json` \u2014 source_path `README.md`, source_sha256 `737997cf5b7d4129f12ed5485ebbdd5e9d2ce3859a82ded6ac535d222327b713`, file_sha256 `3ef5dced147170146cc2b91aca3870cf8bfb84f952a8c16262a7175ab018cfbf`, lines 1\u201339, packet sha256 `127efa6f...`? no \u2014 packet `content` sha from tool = `3ef5dced...`; intake packet sha `d794df82...`, philosophy packet sha `22570255...`. Key lines: L3\u20135 public-prototype disclaimer (research prototype, not official DeepSeek product; publication-adapted, not identical to internal version or implementation described in *Exploring Super-agent Design: Towards a More Autonomous Agent System*; some article designs are future directions not implemented); L7 product framing (proactive coding agent for one GitHub repo, DeepSeek Harness bundle, listens to GitHub and optionally Feishu, work item + own session/dir, answers in original conversation, web panel); L9 attention principle; L35 `pnpm check` runs typecheck, tests, build.\\n2. `deepseek_philosophy.json` \u2014 source_path `docs/000-philosophy.md`, source_sha256 `0a12126843556fde2bcc2ca52dae2c297b9b5ca9170c3e33d624b2a4d85ca76b`, lines 1\u201333. Key: L5 attention principle; L11 act only when asked/rule allows; L12 speak only when a person must act or can use result; L13 one concrete question at a time; L14 stop by impact; L15 report honestly; L19 few concepts; L20 few settings; L21 panel shows only what needs a person; L22 documents read in order; L28\u201331 start narrow/tune for less noise/do not produce volume/own what it says; L29 \\\"When the agent is noisy, make its prompts shorter and stricter, or pause it. Do not add more messages to explain the noise.\\\"; L33 goal.\\n3. `deepseek_intake.json` \u2014 source_path `src/core/intake.ts`, source_sha256 `323aadefea69436ba23ed2de3bdbaad673d61915be9e239f3233ecf551a74179`, lines 1\u201363 (class `Intake extends EnginePart`; `receive(received: Trigger): ReceiveResult` with `'stored'|'duplicate'|'filtered'`). Key lines: L21 isoTime normalise; L22 throw if no threads; L23 duplicate by id; L25\u201328 single `options.scope.scope(trigger)`, filtered \u2192 save trigger + disposition `{filtered:{code}, fanout:[], at}` and return `'filtered'`; L31\u201337 thread keys, lastAt monotonic, correlated union excluding self; L38 `thread.subscriptions`; L42\u201345 `followed = !!thread.context?.includes(ticketId)`, `resumes = trigger.human && ticket?.ended?.by !== 'human' && !followed`, skip if `!ticket || (!liveTicket(ticket) && !resumes)`, reached map with context flag staying true only if followed on all paths; L49\u201351 `tickets.addInput` keyed `key('input', ticketId, 'trigger', trigger.id)` with optional human/context tags; L53\u201355 fanout + context subset disposition; L56\u201358 comment: human message no ticket decides (or reaching only human-stopped/context tickets) and every bot's goes to Eval \u2014 `if (!this.owners(trigger).length) this.queueForEval(trigger)`; L59 wake fanout tickets; L60 emit `'trigger.received'`; L61 return `'stored'`.\\n\\nNot supplied: the architecture article itself; definitions of `scope()`, `liveTicket()`, `owners()`/`followupOwners()`, `threadKey()`, `Tickets`/`Trigger`/`Ticket`/`Thread`/`SourceScope` types, `addInput`/`wake` bodies. All such semantics are **inferred from call sites/comments**, not observed definitions.\\n\\n`inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/` contains exactly: `deepseek_intake.json`, `deepseek_philosophy.json`, `deepseek_readme.json`, `scenario.json`. `work/` contained only `quest_84d8b0697f1b`. `scenario.json` (source_sha256 `11b4340adda7e86e380c8611ccce9d06c0dd213272ffa6f99a97e214ddcbeda7`, packet sha `127efa6f...`): L2, checks `actual_framework_sources`, `multi_specialist_analysis`, `exact_source_citations`, `independent_reviewer`; expected_artifacts `research.json`; plus the original prompt text.\\n\\n## Environment / paths (task context)\\n- quest_id `quest_84d8b0697f1b`, run_id `run_50231b652525`, plan_id `plan_66bf122884ec`, workspace_id `a07f5a6a9090f98239068b1d`, cwd `...\\\\data\\\\worker-environments\\\\quest_84d8b0697f1b\\\\run_50231b652525\\\\work`; output dir `...\\\\run_50231b652525\\\\output`; tmp likewise. Deadline 1794781184.0292437 (unix ts). Sandbox: private working directory, `os_sandbox: false`.\\n- Writes we made landed at `D:\\\\Competition_this\\\\Agent\\\\.local\\\\superagent\\\\20261115T220426Z-capability-fixed-6e2553\\\\work\\\\quest_84d8b0697f1b\\\\research.json`; input reads resolved relative to the project root as `inputs/projects/project_beta/l2/...`.\\n\\n## Decisions made and reasons\\n- Used only directly verified line text for quotes; kept line ranges inclusive.\\n- Refused to reconstruct the article from memory; treated the article as absent and labelled article-level claims only as README-characterised (README L3\u20135).\\n- Made no execution claims: everything framed as source inspection; `pnpm check` documented (README L35) but **not run**.\\n- Single self-contained `research.json` under our quest dir so the Architect integrator needn't re-read l2/; inputs untouched.\\n- Projected every top-level claim into the three-way split: (a) public prototype behaviour evidenced by cited intake.ts lines (+README L7), (b) article directions known only via README L3\u20135 (unnamed, unverified), (c) not improvable from the supplied excerpt (article text; scope()/liveTicket()/owners()/followupOwners()/threadKey() definitions; type shapes; any Source-side or content-level correlation beyond id dedup